 "description": "A 200 by 150 foot village compound: four homes open onto market lanes, gardens and a packed-earth ancestral-hall forecourt. Stalls line the lane edges and leave the doors clear. The ancestral hall has stone wall sections (27 HP, AC 17) and a wooden south door (18 HP, AC 15). Open the door or destroy a section to enter; a breach opens only that square. Other building walls are permanent. Rubble costs double movement; low courtyard stones give +2 AC cover. The well, stalls and carts block their squares until destroyed. Both sides start beside the hall forecourt, with north and south flanks.",
